name grass_walk
describe Prompt 007 goal 343. Walks slowly outward from a grass field so both ground-cover tier boundaries -- the raster overlay at 14 m and the voxel blades at 24 m -- cross the frame. Goal 340's ring check is measured on this pose; the capture is what a person looks at.
backend both

# TAA off for every scenario that compares a capture against a golden. Measured, not assumed:
# with TAA on, vk-vs-vk moves 0.996% of pixels at this pose against a 1.5% gate, and with it off
# 0.341% -- see dev/harness/src/image_compare.hpp for the full four-case table.
option --no-taa
# Auto-exposure meters at the CROSSHAIR, and a crosshair aimed at grass a metre away is a dark
# subject: the first attempt at this shot came back a white frame.
option --no-auto-exposure
option --grass-overlay
# Both boundaries in one frame: a near-level pose puts 14 m and 24 m into rows 335 and 301 of a
# 720-row image, so a ring would read as a horizontal band.
option --no-wind

pose_ground 0,0 90 -9 1.7
wait 3

capture end grass_walk no-golden

assert frames > 0
assert contrast_percent > 6
